+## 3. Blast radius of the `POOR` state (why the output guard came first)
+
+| Consumer | Behaviour on `POOR` |
+|---|---|
+| `api/services/resistance_prophet/test_router.py:171` | logs `PROGNOSIS_ALERT` at CRITICAL and appends an **IMMEDIATE `LOW_PASS_WGS`** `NextTestAction`. `TestRouter` is production-wired via `api/services/ayesha_care_plan/resistance_service.py:16,29,256` |
+| `api/services/next_test_recommender.py:248-261` | inserts a priority-1 lp-WGS recommendation on `resistance_prediction["prognosis"]["status"] == "POOR"` |
+| `api/services/resistance_prophet/shim.py:118` | serialises the dataclass via `asdict`, key `state` |
+
+**Latent shape bug found while tracing this (record as a separate item, not fixed here):**
+`next_test_recommender.py` reads `prognosis["status"]`, but `shim.py:118` serialises the field
+as `state`. `prognosis.get("status", "UNKNOWN")` therefore never equals `"POOR"` and that
+branch is dead on the serialised path. Additionally
+`complete_care_universal.py:1131-1137` calls `get_next_test_recommendations(...)` **without**
+`resistance_prediction`, so on that route the branch cannot fire at all; only the `:1412`
+call site passes `resistance_prediction=`. Do not "fix" the key name without re-reviewing
+whether the recommendation is wanted — renaming `status` to `state` would *activate* a
+currently-dead care-influencing path.
+
